  "summary": "This study compares three fabricated Ti3C2Tx-based electrodes: KOH-mediated 3D porous Ti3C2Tx, a vacuum-filtered Ti3C2Tx control, and a porous Ti3C2Tx/partially reduced GO (M/G) composite. The porous Ti3C2Tx film was produced by reduced-repulsion freeze-casting, while KOH modified its surface chemistry and enabled an ordered porous network. Its best reported gravimetric capacitance was 358.8 F g\u22121 at 20 mV s\u22121; the high-loading 16.18 mg cm\u22122 film reached 3731 mF cm\u22122 at 10 mV s\u22121. Numerical electrode thickness, BET area, porosity, tortuosity, and lateral flake size were not reported in the supplied text."
